{"tool_name":"renano","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"renano","home":"https://github.com/guilledufort/RENANO","license":"MIT","summary":"RENANO is a reference-based lossless FASTQ data compressor, specifically tailored to compress FASTQ files generated with nanopore sequencing technologies. RENANO improves on its state of the art predecessor ENANO, by providing a more efficient base call sequence compression component. Two compression algorithms are introduced, corresponding to the following scenarios: (1) a reference genome is available without cost to both the compressor and the decompressor; (2) the reference genome is available only on the compressor side, and a compacted version of the reference is included in the compressed file.","addition_date":"2021-11-29T09:59:46.613233Z","last_update_date":"2021-11-29T09:59:46.615871Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:renano","credit":[{"email":"almartin@fing.edu.uy","name":"\u00c1lvaro Mart\u00edn","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8601-1242","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Base-calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3185"},{"term":"Parsing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_1812"},{"term":"Sequence trimming","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3192"}]}],"name":"RENANO","owner":"Kigaard","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/2021.03.26.437155"}],"topic":[{"term":"DNA polymorphism","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2885"},{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0102"},{"term":"Metagenomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3174"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"RENANO","home":"https://bio.tools/renano","license":"MIT","summary":"RENANO is a reference-based lossless FASTQ data compressor, specifically tailored to compress FASTQ files generated with nanopore sequencing technologies. RENANO improves on its state of the ar